From: pandabon <pandabon@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boards: spike, chipyard: use schema-valid twister type/simulation

spike_riscv64.yaml declares `type: spike` and `simulation: - name: spike`,
neither of which the twister platform schema accepts
(scripts/schemas/twister/platform-schema.yaml). Twister validates every
board it discovers, so any `west twister` run in a workspace containing
this board aborts with "Schema validation failed", even for other boards.

Use the schema's existing values: spike_riscv64 becomes `type: sim` with
`simulation: custom` / `exec: spike`; the chipyard_* boards (real chips,
`type: chipyard`, `simulation: chipyard`) become `type: mcu` with the invalid
simulation entry dropped, i.e. hardware boards (twister builds them only).

NOT APPLIED. Proposed for the ucb-bar/zephyr fork; apply with
  git -C zephyr apply zephyr-chipyard-bsp/patches/zephyr/0004-boards-spike-fix-twister-platform-schema.patch
---diff --git a/boards/chipyard/arty/chipyard_arty.yaml b/boards/chipyard/arty/chipyard_arty.yaml
index 5f2eee6..fa6467c 100644
--- a/boards/chipyard/arty/chipyard_arty.yaml
+++ b/boards/chipyard/arty/chipyard_arty.yaml
@@ -1,8 +1,6 @@
 identifier: chipyard_arty
 name: Chipyard Generated RISCV SoCs 
-type: chipyard 
-simulation:
-  - name: chipyard
+type: mcu
 arch: riscv
 toolchain:
   - zephyr
